{"id": "6c8721df-616c-4407-8595-9604d5d1e390", "timestamp": "2026-10-21T23:36:02.889908", "source": "agent", "parent_id": "92c2bb66-962e-4c5e-ac1b-13e08d8ccb76", "action": null, "tool_name": "end_researcher_turn", "tool_call_id": "call-8c1af990-e11a-4c43-ac9d-aa9f978b5c4b", "tool_call": {"id": "call-8c1af990-e11a-4c43-ac9d-aa9f978b5c4b", "responses_item_id": null, "name": "end_researcher_turn", "arguments": "{\"summary\":\"Propose plan for MinED vs EM on BBH Alignment\",\"stage\":\"plan\",\"answer\":\"Plan for a design-only comparison of MinED vs EM under the Alignment criterion on BBH. The sandbox contains only task.json; no source paper, no model, no data. The deliverable at the result stage will be a faithful, source-anchored experimental design (hypothesis, variables, materials, procedure, statistics, controls, threats-to-validity) with NO fabricated numbers and NO claim that an experiment was run. The plan above (i) defines what I mean by MinED, EM, BBH, and \\\"Alignment Criteria\\\" as flagged working assumptions, (ii) proposes holding every variable constant except the decoding rule, (iii) pre-registers a paired statistical analysis (paired bootstrap + Wilcoxon + McNemar) across the 23 BBH tasks with a pre-specified \\\"outperforms\\\" rule, (iv) lists feasibility checks and a negative control, and (v) enumerates six uncertainties (paper's exact definition of Alignment, exact definitions of MinED vs EM, base LLM, official hyperparameters, per-BBH-sub-category stratification, prompt-set source) that I would like the researcher to confirm before producing the final design. Awaiting the researcher's approval before proceeding to the full design document.\",\"evidence\":\"Workspace check: `ls /workspace` shows only `task.json`; recursive listing confirms no subdirectories or files. `find / -maxdepth 2 -name '*.pdf' -o -name '*.md'` returns no matches other than the task file. `python3 --version` reports Python 3.12.3 with no project dependencies preinstalled. task.json contains the question and a single line of context: \\\"Design-only task; repositories and compute are not required.\\\" The researcher_topics list references ICLR 2024 paper 18013 setup topics (setup_2, 4, 10, 11, 14, 15), but no PDF or supplementary material from that paper is bundled in the sandbox, and network is disabled, so I cannot fetch it from inside. Consequently the design must (a) treat the paper's terminology as TBD pending researcher confirmation, (b) state all assumptions explicitly, and (c) stop short of any execution or numerical claim, matching the researcher's explicit instruction.\",\"assumptions\":[\"MinED = Minimum-Entropy Decoding, a training-free contrastive decoding rule that selects tokens minimizing the output-entropy (or a contrast lower/upper entropy) factor; treated as a decoding-only change of the selection rule applied to an existing LLM.</item>\\n<item>EM method = \\\"Entropy-Maximization\\\" decoding, the symmetric/baseline counterpart whose only difference from MinED is the sign of the entropy term; identical inference budget and prompts.</item>\\n\"],\"uncertainties\":[{\"item\":{\"item\":{\"item\":{\"item\":{\"item\":\"Helpful: which BBH prompt source the paper licenses the few-shot CoT prompts and evaluation harness from (lukaemon/bbh, OpenCompass bb, HELM, etc.).</item>\",\"$text\":\"Helpful: whether the paper stratifies BBH results into sub-categories (algorithmic vs. semantic) — design should mirror that stratification if so.</item>\"},\"$text\":\"Helpful: official hyper-parameters for MinED and EM on BBH as reported in the paper, so they can be held fixed rather than re-tuned.</item>\"},\"$text\":\"Required: which base LLM the paper used to evaluate BBH (drives reproducibility and hyper-parameter interpretation).</item>\"},\"$text\":\"Required: paper's exact operative definitions of MinED and EM (training-free decoders vs. training/alignment methods) — if they are training-based rather than decoder-only, the controls in the design must change.</item>\"},\"$text\":\"Required: paper's exact definition of \\\"Alignment Criteria\\\" (BBH exact-match vs. a paper-specific axis vs. human-rated alignment).</item>\"}]}", "origin": "completion"}, "llm_response_id": "chatcmpl-b77142fb-09f3-4e6c-a7e8-a9915893b020", "security_risk": "UNKNOWN", "kind": "ActionEvent", "source_event_index": 12}
