{"id": "4c975a7a-9d6f-4668-9aa1-6ca6c41cd9cf", "timestamp": "2026-10-21T23:36:54.920963", "source": "user", "parent_id": "c766e5e9-d56d-4d52-92f0-f96b505aa202", "llm_message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"cache_prompt": false, "type": "text", "text": "{\"researcher_request\": \"The plan is sensible in skeleton (paired design across the 23 BBH tasks, controls for prompt/model/budget, pre-registered paired bootstrap + Wilcoxon + McNemar, no fabrication, design-only), but it misreads two of the fixed requirements you should treat as authoritative. Please revise before I can approve the approach. Two corrections: (1) The study context lists EM and MinED under fixed_requirement IDs iclr2024/18013/4:setup_10 and :setup_11, and they define EM as Exact Matching and MinED as Minimum Edit Distance. These are post-hoc alignment/scoring criteria applied to compare model outputs against gold answers, not contrastive decoding algorithms. Your working assumption that 'MinED = Minimum-Entropy Decoding' and 'EM = an Entropy-Maximization decoding baseline' therefore contradicts setup_10 and setup_11 and must be replaced. (2) Consequently the independent variable is not a decoding hyper-parameter but a matching criterion applied to identical model outputs; the manipulation is purely at the scoring stage, which removes concerns about retuning decoding and changes what 'holding all else constant' means. Please redraw the design with this corrected operationalization: same frozen LLM, same fixed CoT prompts, same sampled outputs, same BBH 23+4 task list; only the matching rule changes. Keep the paired statistical plan and the pre-specified outperforms rule, but restate them now in terms of alignment-criterion accuracy (e.g., MC exact match for the 23 MC tasks and a Normalized Edit Distance score for the 4 free-form tasks). Confirm in your revised plan that you have dropped the decoding-rule framing, that you accept setup_10 and setup_11 as authoritative, and that the negative control is rerunning scoring under EM as a sanity check on the MinED code path. Once those are corrected and re-submitted as the approach, I will approve.\", \"required_handoff_stage\": \"plan\", \"approach_approved\": false}"}], "tool_calls": null, "tool_call_id": null, "name": null}, "llm_response_id": null, "activated_skills": [], "extended_content": [], "sender": null, "kind": "MessageEvent", "source_event_index": 18}
