{"id": "1034b8bc-080c-4808-9468-11d7bc7fec44", "timestamp": "2026-10-21T23:38:28.315634", "source": "user", "parent_id": "1f30b1d8-97ea-4141-892c-6f1191e15e17", "llm_message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"cache_prompt": false, "type": "text", "text": "{\"researcher_request\": \"Approved. Your corrected framing, in which setup_10 (EM = Exact Matching) and setup_11 (MinED = Minimum Edit Distance) are treated as authoritative, the decoding-rule interpretation is fully retracted, and the independent variable is restricted to the evaluation-time scoring criterion over identical frozen model outputs, is consistent with the fixed requirements and with the design-only deliverable contract. I accept the paired within-instance design over the 23 MC + 4 free-form BBH tasks, the two pre-specified operational definitions of outperforms (A: gradedness/discrimination; B: agreement with a quality proxy), the paired statistical stack (per-task paired bootstrap on task-level Deltas, Wilcoxon signed-rank as robustness, McNemar-style sign test for definition B, with task-type stratification between the 23 MC and the 4 free-form subsets and family-wise handling applied separately to A and B), and the mandatory negative control in which the MinED code path is collapsed to EM and required to match within machine precision on every task. Because the paper PDF is not available inside this sandbox and the network is disabled, residual factual details (tokenization choice for MinED, base LLM identity, exact BBH task list, whether A or B is the papers primary operationalization, and any pre-specified effect-size threshold) are to be carried forward as flagged working assumptions to be sourced at compile time rather than filled in by us; please label them explicitly as TBD-by-source so they remain auditable. Please now produce the final design document. Structure it as: (1) Hypothesis and operationalization of outperforms (both definitions A and B, with explicit primary and secondary); (2) Variables and controls (frozen model, greedy decoding, identical CoT prompts, identical generations, identical max-new-tokens, RNG seed, the only manipulation at scoring); (3) Materials (BBH task list grouped by MC vs free-form, prompt source as TBD-by-source, predicted-text cache as the single shared artifact); (4) Procedure for the two scoring passes and the negative control; (5) Analysis plan with the full paired statistical stack, stratification, multiple-comparison handling, and pre-registered thresholds; (6) Threats to validity (tokenization sensitivity, prompt-template drift, free-form answer extraction, machine-precision determinism, multiple-comparison, ecological validity of the chosen proxy); (7) Feasibility (no execution required, design-only, expected memory and runtime of the planned stack on a single CPU, what would change if executed). Use only what is source-supported or explicitly flagged as a working assumption; do not fabricate any numerical result and do not state or imply that the experiment was executed. Final field must satisfy the submission contract for a design-only deliverable.\", \"required_handoff_stage\": \"result\", \"approach_approved\": true}"}], "tool_calls": null, "tool_call_id": null, "name": null}, "llm_response_id": null, "activated_skills": [], "extended_content": [], "sender": null, "kind": "MessageEvent", "source_event_index": 21}
{"id": "ab78313c-3d5e-48ed-882f-e4e5b555e10f", "timestamp": "2026-10-21T23:40:36.509203", "source": "agent", "parent_id": "1034b8bc-080c-4808-9468-11d7bc7fec44", "action": {"stage": "result", "answer": "# Design Document — Does MinED (Minimum Edit Distance) outperform EM (Exact Matching) as the Alignment criterion on BBH?\n\n**Deliverable type:** Design only. No execution. No numerical result is reported or implied.\n\n**Authoritative bindings (unchanged from approved plan):**\n- `setup_10`: EM = Exact Matching.\n- `setup_11`: MinED = Minimum Edit Distance.\n- Both are evaluation-time scoring criteria, applied to identical frozen model outputs. The manipulation sits at the scoring step only.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Hypothesis and operationalization of \"outperforms\"\n\n### 1.1 Substantive hypothesis\nOn the BBH evaluation set used by the paper (23 multiple-choice tasks + 4 free-form tasks, **`TBD-by-source`** for the exact list and category assignment), the **Minimum Edit Distance (MinED) alignment score is a more faithful alignment criterion than the Exact Match (EM) score**, when both scores are computed on the same frozen model-generated strings.\n\n### 1.2 Why raw-mean comparison is undefined\nBy construction, on any paired instance `i`, `mined_i ≥ em_i`, because MinED = 1 when `em_i = 1` (zero edits) and gives partial credit when `em_i = 0`. Therefore the question **cannot** be resolved by comparing means of the two score distributions. Two non-trivial operationalizations are pre-registered instead.\n\n### 1.3 Operational definition A — Gradedness / discriminative power (PRIMARY)\n> MinED outperforms EM if, across the BBH instances, MinED distributes mass over more distinct score values and exhibits higher resolvable variance than EM, and that extra resolution concentrates on the 4 free-form tasks where partial-credit distinctions are meaningful.\n- Per-task: distinct-value count, entropy of the empirical distribution, variance of each score vector.\n- Aggregate: paired bootstrap of `Var_t(MinED) − Var_t(EM)` across the 27 task-level differences.\n\n### 1.4 Operational definition B — Agreement with a quality proxy (SECONDARY)\n> MinED outperforms EM if the `[score_i, quality_proxy_i]` rank association under MinED is strictly stronger than under EM on a strict majority of BBH tasks.\n- Per-task rank association: Kendall's τ-b (with Spearman's ρ as robustness) between the score vector and an external quality proxy `Q_i`.\n- Aggregate: paired bootstrap of `|τ_t(MinED, Q)| − |τ_t(EM, Q)|` across the 27 task-level differences; McNemar-style sign test on the sign of that difference.\n\n### 1.5 Pre-registered primary outcome\nDefinition A is primary because it does not depend on a quality proxy whose choice is itself a paper-specific commitment. Definition B is pre-registered as secondary, contingent on the proxy choice being one that the paper explicitly licenses; on a placeholder-only proxy choice, Definition B is reported but de-emphasized.\n\n### 1.6 Effect-size threshold\n**`TBD-by-source`**: the pre-registered effect-size rule (\"outperforms ⇒ Δ exceeds threshold θ\") is deferred to the paper's own pre-registration. If none is published, a conservative placeholder (Cohen's *d* ≥ 0.5 on Definition A's variance difference; Δ |τ| ≥ 0.10 for Definition B) is recorded as documentation of the slot, **not binding**.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Variables and controls\n\n### 2.1 Independent variable (the only manipulated factor)\n- **Scoring criterion**, two levels: `EM`, `MinED` (MinED tokenization **`TBD-by-source`**: character-level vs. BPE-token-level Levenshtein).\n\n### 2.2 Dependent variables\n- **Per-instance scalar score** `s_i ∈ [0, 1]` produced by each scoring criterion.\n- **Derived:** Definition A uses variance, distinct-value count, entropy of `{s_i}` per task; Definition B uses Kendall's τ-b and Spearman's ρ of `{s_i}` against the quality proxy `{q_i}` per task.\n- **Aggregate:** macro-mean across the 27 BBH tasks, with stratification by task type (23 MC vs. 4 free-form).\n\n### 2.3 Frozen control variables (identical across both scoring passes)\n| Control | Value / Source | Status |\n|---|---|---|\n| Base LLM weights | Paper-specified backbone | `TBD-by-source` |\n| Tokenizer & chat template | Paper-specified | `TBD-by-source` |\n| Decoding strategy | Greedy (temperature = 0, no top-k / top-p / sampling) | fixed in design |\n| RNG seed | Single fixed seed | fixed in design |\n| Max-new-tokens | Paper-specified cap | `TBD-by-source` |\n| CoT prompt templates | Paper-specified BBH prompts | fixed by source |\n| Number of shots | 3 (BBH canonical) unless paper overrides | fixed in design |\n| **Per-instance predicted text** | A single frozen cache of strings `pred_i` | **single shared artifact** |\n| Gold text | BBH gold references | fixed in design |\n| Answer-extraction regex | One rule for both passes | fixed in design |\n| Hardware | Single CPU thread | fixed in design |\n\nBecause the per-instance predicted text is byte-identical across the two passes, any score difference is attributable solely to the matching rule, **provided** the negative control (§4.3) passes.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Materials\n\n### 3.1 BBH task list and stratification (TBD-by-source for exact subset)\nThe paper's BBH configuration is **23 MC + 4 free-form = 27 total**. The canonical 27-task reference frame (Suzgun et al., 2022) is given below; the **paper-specific subset and category assignment are `TBD-by-source`**:\n\n```\nBoolean Expressions          free-form / boolean string\nCausal Judgement             MC\nDate Understanding           MC\nDisambiguation QA            MC\nFormal Fallacies             MC\nGeometric Shapes             MC\nHyperbaton                   MC\nLogical Deduction (3,5,7)    MC (3 tasks)\nMovie Recommendation         MC\nMultistep Arithmetic         free-form, numeric\nNavigate                     MC (Yes/No)\nObject Counting              free-form, numeric\nPenguins in a Table          free-form, structured\nReasoning about Colored Objects  MC\nRuin Names                   MC\nSalient Translation          free-form (also MC-able)\nSnarks                       MC\nSports Understanding         MC\nTemporal Sequences           MC\nTracking Shuffled Objects    MC (3 tasks: 3, 5, 7)\nWeb of Lies                  MC (Yes/No)\nWord Sorting                 free-form, list\n```\n\n### 3.2 Prompt source (TBD-by-source)\nCandidate sources: `lukaemon/bbh`, original BBH release, `OpenCompass bbh` loader, `HELM` BBH, or paper-supplied JSON. The source matters only insofar as the **same** prompt set is consumed by both scoring passes; any source difference is a confound.\n\n### 3.3 Shared artifact — predicted-text cache\nA single frozen JSONL cache, one record per instance:\n```json\n{\n  \"task\": \"<BBH-task-name, TBD-by-source>\",\n  \"instance_id\": \"<BBH-internal-id>\",\n  \"prompt\": \"<exact CoT prompt sent to the model>\",\n  \"response\": \"<exact decoded continuation>\",\n  \"extracted_answer\": \"<answer string after paper's extraction regex>\",\n  \"gold\": \"<BBH gold reference>\",\n  \"seed\": <int>,\n  \"temperature\": 0\n}\n```\nThis cache is the **single shared artifact** for both scoring passes, guaranteeing identical bytes compared, identical chat-template application, identical answer extraction for EM.\n\n### 3.4 Planned stack (design-only)\n- Python 3.12.3.\n- MinED via Levenshtein (`python-Levenshtein` if offline-installable; pure-Python `O(nm)` DP fallback otherwise). Tokenization **`TBD-by-source`**.\n- Statistics: `numpy` paired bootstrap, `scipy.stats.wilcoxon`, `kendalltau`, `spearmanr`, custom sign test. CIs via percentile bootstrap, 10,000 resamples on the 27 task-differences.\n- No GPU; no model-inference runtime required at scoring time.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Procedure\n\n### 4.1 Pass 1 — Build the predicted-text cache\nFor each task in the 23+4 list and each instance within:\n1. Build the CoT prompt `P_{t,i}` from the paper's prompt source.\n2. Run the base LLM greedily (temperature 0, fixed seed), with the paper's max-new-tokens cap.\n3. Record `(prompt, response, extracted_answer)` and the gold reference into the JSONL cache.\n\nThe cache is **scoring-agnostic**: both passes below consume it and never call the model.\n\n### 4.2 Pass 2 — EM scoring pass\n1. For each record `r`, normalize `r.extracted_answer` and `r.gold` (lowercase, strip whitespace, collapse internal whitespace; normalization rule `TBD-by-source` to mirror the paper).\n2. `em_i = 1` if normalized predicted `==` normalized gold, else `0`.\n3. Per-task aggregate: `mean_t(em)`, `var_t(em)`, distinct-value count, empirical entropy.\n4. MC tasks: compare canonical option letters; free-form tasks: compare the post-extraction string. Same rule for both scoring passes — fixing only the EM target string.\n\n### 4.3 Pass 3 — MinED scoring pass (with mandatory negative control)\n**Standard MinED pass.**\n1. For each record `r`, tokenize `r.extracted_answer` and `r.gold` per the paper's MinED tokenization (`TBD-by-source`).\n2. Compute Levenshtein distance `d_i` over the chosen tokens.\n3. `mined_i = 1 − d_i / max(len(pred_tokens), len(gold_tokens))`, clamped to `[0, 1]`. Empty-string guards `TBD-by-source`.\n4. Per-task aggregate: `mean_t(mined)`, `var_t(mined)`, distinct-value count, empirical entropy.\n\n**Mandatory negative control — forced-EM rerun of the MinED code path.**\nRe-execute the MinED code with the Levenshtein DP replaced by an exact-equality token comparison (zero distance iff `pred_tokens == gold_tokens`, else a value that makes `1 − d/max(·) = 0`). Result: on every instance, every task, `mined_forced_i == em_i` to machine precision. Any discrepancy halts the experiment with an error report.\n\n**Tokenization sensitivity appendix (robustness only).**\nRepeat the MinED pass with both character-level and BPE-token-level Levenshtein (the two natural choices for the paper's tokenizer); record discrepancy. **Not** used for primary inference; **only** to expose sensitivity to the `TBD-by-source` choice.\n\n### 4.4 Pass 4 — Quality-proxy scoring (Definition B only)\nIf a paper-licensed proxy exists:\n1. For each record, compute `q_i` per the paper's definition (candidates `TBD-by-source`: log-prob of gold under the frozen LLM; multi-sample echo agreement; human-rated subset).\n2. Pair `q_i` with `em_i` and `mined_i` per instance.\n\n### 4.5 Pass 5 — Aggregate and infer (no execution performed)\nSee §5.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Analysis plan\n\n### 5.1 Unit of pairing\nEvery comparison is **paired on instance `i`**. For each instance, both `em_i` and `mined_i` are available; for Definition B, `q_i` is additionally available.\n\n### 5.2 Definition A — discriminative power\n- Per task `t`: `Δ^{A}_t = Var_t(MinED) − Var_t(EM)`; auxiliary `Δ^{A,ent}_t`, `Δ^{A,card}_t`.\n- Across the 27 tasks:\n  - **Primary**: paired bootstrap, 10,000 resamples, percentile 95% CI on mean `Δ^{A}_t` (tasks resampled with replacement).\n  - **Robustness**: Wilcoxon signed-rank on `Δ^{A}_t`.\n- **Stratification**: separately for the 23-task MC subset and the 4-task free-form subset; reported descriptively and inferentially as sub-family tests (n = 4 treated descriptively on its own).\n\n### 5.3 Definition B — agreement with a quality proxy\n- Per task `t`: `τ^{EM}_t = KendallTau_b(em_t, q_t)`, `τ^{MIN}_t = KendallTau_b(mined_t, q_t)`; `Δ^{B}_t = |τ^{MIN}_t| − |τ^{EM}_t|`.\n- **Primary**: paired bootstrap (10,000 resamples) of mean `Δ^{B}_t` across the 27 tasks; percentile 95% CI.\n- **Robustness**: Wilcoxon signed-rank on `Δ^{B}_t`; sign test on `sign(Δ^{B}_t)` (McNemar-style).\n- **Stratification**: identical to Definition A.\n\n### 5.4 Multiple-comparison handling\n- A and B are reported in **separate families**; no pooled family-wise test across them.\n- Within each family, the three statistics are descriptively reported; only the **primary** statistic's bootstrap CI carries the inferential claim.\n- Subset analyses are descriptive; no post-hoc adjustments are pre-registered.\n\n### 5.5 Pre-registered decision rule (TBD-by-source)\nDefer to the paper. Placeholder rules, **not binding**:\n- Definition A: declare if 95% CI on mean `Δ^{A}_t` is strictly above 0 and Wilcoxon two-sided `p ≤ 0.05` with rank-biserial ≥ 0.5.\n- Definition B: declare if 95% CI on mean `Δ^{B}_t` is strictly above 0 and sign test two-sided `p ≤ 0.05`.\n\n### 5.6 Result-section structure (no numbers)\n1. Negative-control outcome (forced-EM == EM must hold).\n2. Definition A per-task deltas, stratification, bootstrap CI, Wilcoxon `p`.\n3. Definition B per-task deltas, sign test; reported as \"incomplete\" if no paper-licensed proxy exists.\n4. Tokenization-sensitivity appendix.\n5. Threats-to-validity walk-through before any interpretive claim.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Threats to validity\n1. **Tokenization sensitivity for MinED (char vs. BPE).** Mitigated by the dual-pass robustness appendix; the paper's choice is mirrored as the primary.\n2. **Prompt-template drift across scoring passes.** Mitigated by the same prompt source and the frozen JSONL cache that records `prompt` per record.\n3. **Free-form answer-extraction aggressiveness.** A single fixed extraction regex feeds both passes, so the bias cancels within-pairs but conditions absolute magnitudes. Documented.\n4. **Machine-precision determinism.** The forced-EM negative control is the primary defense; LSB-level disagreement is treated as a coding bug, halts inference. Greedy decoding makes cache-build reproducible.\n5. **Multiple-comparison pollution across A, B, and stratified subsets.** A and B are separate families; within-family primary-statistic discipline; stratification treated descriptively.\n6. **Ecological validity of the quality proxy (Definition B).** Definition B is secondary to a proxy-free Definition A; proxies are kept `TBD-by-source`; if no proxy is paper-licensed, Definition B is reported as \"incomplete\".\n7. **Construction bias from `MinED ≥ EM`.** The design refuses raw-mean comparison; Definition A pre-registered as primary; explicit guardrail in §7 of the experimental protocol.\n8. **Single-model / single-seed conditioning.** Results are conditional on paper's LLM and seed; cross-family generalization is out of scope.\n9. **Empty-string and tie-handling edge cases in MinED.** Guards `TBD-by-source` from paper; edge cases enumerated.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Feasibility\n\n### 7.1 Status\nDesign-only. **No experiment has been executed. No command in this document is asserted to have been run.** The sandbox contains only `task.json`; no source PDF, no model weights, no dataset, no project dependencies installed.\n\n### 7.2 Scoring-stage feasibility on a single CPU\n- **Per-pair Levenshtein**: `O(L_pred·L_gold)` time, `O(min(L_pred, L_gold))` memory (rolling-row). For BBH, `L_pred, L_gold ≲ max_new_tokens` — sub-millisecond per instance in pure Python.\n- **Per-task aggregate**: linear in `(num_instances × L_pred × L_gold)`; tens of seconds wall-clock per task for both passes on a single thread, given typical ~250 instances per task.\n- **Bootstrap**: 10,000 resamples × 27 tasks × `O(|task|)` reduction; a few minutes wall-clock; no GPU.\n- **Memory**: predicted-text cache a few MB; Levenshtein DP negligible; bootstrap holding `10,000 × 27` floats negligible.\n- All operations are CPU-friendly, FFT-free, no parallel prefix-sums. **Single-CPU correctness is feasible and well-defined.**\n\n### 7.3 What would change if executed (out of scope)\n- Pass 1 (cache build) is the heavy step: minutes-to-hours on CPU for a 7B-class model, hours-to-days on a GPU cluster for 70B-class. It scales with model size. **This design does not run it.**\n- If the paper specifies multi-seed / multi-temperature averaging, the design would draw a fixed seed from the paper's pre-registration rather than inventing one; `TBD-by-source`.\n- Definition B is gated on the paper-licensed quality proxy; without one, Definition B is reported as \"incomplete\".\n- `scipy`/`numpy` not pre-installed and bubblewrap forbids installation in this submission, so even a feasibility validation run is out of scope here.\n\n### 7.4 Submission-contract statement\n- **No result is claimed.** The deliverable is a design document, not an experimental report.\n- **No computation is asserted to have happened.** All numbers in the protocol are structural (counts of tasks, asymptotic costs, decision-rule placeholders).\n- **All paper-specific facts are flagged `TBD-by-source`**: MinED tokenization, base LLM, exact 23+4 split, Definition-A-vs-B primary, pre-registered effect-size threshold, quality proxy, seed/temperature policy.\n- **The decoding-rule framing is fully retracted.** The independent variable sits only at the scoring step on identical frozen model outputs.\n- **The negative control is mandated before any inference.** A failed negative control halts the experiment by contract.\n\n---\n\n### Carry-forward compile-time list (`TBD-by-source`, auditable)\n1. MinED tokenization rule (character vs. BPE-token Levenshtein).\n2. Base LLM identity for BBH cache build.\n3. Exact BBH 23+4 task list and category assignment.\n4. BBH prompt source (`lukaemon/bbh`, `OpenCompass`, `HELM`, paper-supplied).\n5. Whether Definition A or Definition B is the paper's primary operationalization of \"outperforms\".\n6. Pre-registered effect-size threshold and decision rule.\n7. Quality proxy for Definition B (log-prob-of-gold / multi-sample echo agreement / human-rated subset).\n8. Seed-and-temperature policy (single fixed vs. seed-averaged).\n\nThis completes the design. Submitting for review.", "evidence": "Re-inspected /workspace; still contains only task.json. No PDF, no supplementary, no model weights, no datasets, no installed project dependencies are available. Network is disabled in the bubblewrap sandbox so the paper PDF for ICLR 2024 ID 18013 cannot be fetched from inside; consequently every paper-specific fact is marked TBD-by-source and bound to the paper, never substituted by the design. The approved plan accepted setup_10 (EM = Exact Matching) and setup_11 (MinED = Minimum Edit Distance) as authoritative scoring criteria, retracted the prior decoding-rule framing, and committed to a paired within-instance design over a 23 MC + 4 free-form BBH split with two pre-registered operational definitions of outperforms (A: gradedness/discrimination as primary; B: agreement with a quality proxy as secondary), a paired bootstrap on task-level Deltas with Wilcoxon as robustness and a McNemar-style sign test for B, stratification by task type, family-wise handling for A vs B, and a mandatory negative control in which the MinED code path is collapsed to EM and required to match within machine precision on every task. The deliverable above implements that plan as a complete design document organized into the seven sections the researcher requested (hypothesis and operationalization; variables and controls; materials including BBH task list, prompt source, and shared predicted-text cache; procedure for the EM pass, the MinED pass, and the forced-EM negative control; paired analysis plan with stratification and multiple-comparison handling plus a TBD-by-source decision rule; threats to validity covering all six items the researcher named plus construction bias and single-model conditioning; and feasibility showing single-CPU correctness with a sub-millisecond per-pair Levenshtein, a few-MB cache, and a few-minute bootstrap). No number is presented as if from a run; no command is asserted to have been executed; every paper-bound element is flagged TBD-by-source and listed once more at the end for auditability.", "assumptions": ["MinED is operationalized here as a normalized Levenshtein alignment score, of the form 1 - edit_distance(predicted, gold) / max(len(predicted), len(gold)), with the edit-distance tokenization (character vs. BPE token) flagged TBD-by-source to mirror the paper.", "EM is operationalized as an exact-match indicator on the normalized final extracted answer string vs. the gold string, returning 1 on equality and 0 otherwise; for MC tasks the canonical option-letter comparison is used.", "BBH evaluation set is operationalized as the papers 23 MC + 4 free-form configuration with the canonical 27-task reference frame (Suzgun et al., 2022) used only as a default enumeration; the exact paper-specific subset and category assignment are flagged TBD-by-source.", "Manipulation is restricted to the scoring step, with all generation-time variables (LLM weights, greedy decoding, CoT 3-shot prompt templates, max-new-tokens, RNG seed, per-instance predicted text bytes) held byte-identical across the two scoring passes.", "Definition A (gradedness/discrimination) is the pre-registered primary operationalization of outperforms because it does not depend on a quality proxy whose choice is itself paper-specific; Definition B (agreement with a quality proxy) is pre-registered as secondary.", "The forced-EM rerun of the MinED code path is treated as a strict pass-or-halt gate rather than a soft check; any disagreement with the original EM pass anywhere on BBH halts the experiment by contract."], "uncertainties": ["TBD-by-source: tokenization rule for MinED (character-level vs. BPE-token-level Levenshtein).", "TBD-by-source: identity of the base LLM frozen for BBH cache build.", "TBD-by-source: exact BBH 23 + 4 task list and category assignment.", "TBD-by-source: BBH prompt source (lukaemon/bbh, OpenCompass, HELM, paper-supplied).", "TBD-by-source: whether the papers primary operationalization of outperforms is Definition A or Definition B.", "TBD-by-source: pre-registered effect-size threshold and decision rule for the outperforms call.", "TBD-by-source: which quality proxy (log-prob-of-gold, multi-sample echo agreement, human-rated subset) the paper licenses for Definition B.", "TBD-by-source: seed-and-temperature policy (single fixed vs. seed-averaged) for the frozen generations."], "kind": "ReviewHandoffAction"}, "tool_name": "end_researcher_turn", "tool_call_id": "call-7802fcf4-dcc6-4749-82ce-415f71f1b210", "tool_call": {"id": "call-7802fcf4-dcc6-4749-82ce-415f71f1b210", "responses_item_id": null, "name": "end_researcher_turn", "arguments": "{\"summary\": \"Final design document for MinED vs EM on BBH\", \"stage\": \"result\", \"answer\": \"# Design Document \\u2014 Does MinED (Minimum Edit Distance) outperform EM (Exact Matching) as the Alignment criterion on BBH?\\n\\n**Deliverable type:** Design only. No execution. No numerical result is reported or implied.\\n\\n**Authoritative bindings (unchanged from approved plan):**\\n- `setup_10`: EM = Exact Matching.\\n- `setup_11`: MinED = Minimum Edit Distance.\\n- Both are evaluation-time scoring criteria, applied to identical frozen model outputs. The manipulation sits at the scoring step only.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. Hypothesis and operationalization of \\\"outperforms\\\"\\n\\n### 1.1 Substantive hypothesis\\nOn the BBH evaluation set used by the paper (23 multiple-choice tasks + 4 free-form tasks, **`TBD-by-source`** for the exact list and category assignment), the **Minimum Edit Distance (MinED) alignment score is a more faithful alignment criterion than the Exact Match (EM) score**, when both scores are computed on the same frozen model-generated strings.\\n\\n### 1.2 Why raw-mean comparison is undefined\\nBy construction, on any paired instance `i`, `mined_i \\u2265 em_i`, because MinED = 1 when `em_i = 1` (zero edits) and gives partial credit when `em_i = 0`. Therefore the question **cannot** be resolved by comparing means of the two score distributions. Two non-trivial operationalizations are pre-registered instead.\\n\\n### 1.3 Operational definition A \\u2014 Gradedness / discriminative power (PRIMARY)\\n> MinED outperforms EM if, across the BBH instances, MinED distributes mass over more distinct score values and exhibits higher resolvable variance than EM, and that extra resolution concentrates on the 4 free-form tasks where partial-credit distinctions are meaningful.\\n- Per-task: distinct-value count, entropy of the empirical distribution, variance of each score vector.\\n- Aggregate: paired bootstrap of `Var_t(MinED) \\u2212 Var_t(EM)` across the 27 task-level differences.\\n\\n### 1.4 Operational definition B \\u2014 Agreement with a quality proxy (SECONDARY)\\n> MinED outperforms EM if the `[score_i, quality_proxy_i]` rank association under MinED is strictly stronger than under EM on a strict majority of BBH tasks.\\n- Per-task rank association: Kendall's \\u03c4-b (with Spearman's \\u03c1 as robustness) between the score vector and an external quality proxy `Q_i`.\\n- Aggregate: paired bootstrap of `|\\u03c4_t(MinED, Q)| \\u2212 |\\u03c4_t(EM, Q)|` across the 27 task-level differences; McNemar-style sign test on the sign of that difference.\\n\\n### 1.5 Pre-registered primary outcome\\nDefinition A is primary because it does not depend on a quality proxy whose choice is itself a paper-specific commitment. Definition B is pre-registered as secondary, contingent on the proxy choice being one that the paper explicitly licenses; on a placeholder-only proxy choice, Definition B is reported but de-emphasized.\\n\\n### 1.6 Effect-size threshold\\n**`TBD-by-source`**: the pre-registered effect-size rule (\\\"outperforms \\u21d2 \\u0394 exceeds threshold \\u03b8\\\") is deferred to the paper's own pre-registration. If none is published, a conservative placeholder (Cohen's *d* \\u2265 0.5 on Definition A's variance difference; \\u0394 |\\u03c4| \\u2265 0.10 for Definition B) is recorded as documentation of the slot, **not binding**.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. Variables and controls\\n\\n### 2.1 Independent variable (the only manipulated factor)\\n- **Scoring criterion**, two levels: `EM`, `MinED` (MinED tokenization **`TBD-by-source`**: character-level vs. BPE-token-level Levenshtein).\\n\\n### 2.2 Dependent variables\\n- **Per-instance scalar score** `s_i \\u2208 [0, 1]` produced by each scoring criterion.\\n- **Derived:** Definition A uses variance, distinct-value count, entropy of `{s_i}` per task; Definition B uses Kendall's \\u03c4-b and Spearman's \\u03c1 of `{s_i}` against the quality proxy `{q_i}` per task.\\n- **Aggregate:** macro-mean across the 27 BBH tasks, with stratification by task type (23 MC vs. 4 free-form).\\n\\n### 2.3 Frozen control variables (identical across both scoring passes)\\n| Control | Value / Source | Status |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Base LLM weights | Paper-specified backbone | `TBD-by-source` |\\n| Tokenizer & chat template | Paper-specified | `TBD-by-source` |\\n| Decoding strategy | Greedy (temperature = 0, no top-k / top-p / sampling) | fixed in design |\\n| RNG seed | Single fixed seed | fixed in design |\\n| Max-new-tokens | Paper-specified cap | `TBD-by-source` |\\n| CoT prompt templates | Paper-specified BBH prompts | fixed by source |\\n| Number of shots | 3 (BBH canonical) unless paper overrides | fixed in design |\\n| **Per-instance predicted text** | A single frozen cache of strings `pred_i` | **single shared artifact** |\\n| Gold text | BBH gold references | fixed in design |\\n| Answer-extraction regex | One rule for both passes | fixed in design |\\n| Hardware | Single CPU thread | fixed in design |\\n\\nBecause the per-instance predicted text is byte-identical across the two passes, any score difference is attributable solely to the matching rule, **provided** the negative control (\\u00a74.3) passes.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. Materials\\n\\n### 3.1 BBH task list and stratification (TBD-by-source for exact subset)\\nThe paper's BBH configuration is **23 MC + 4 free-form = 27 total**. The canonical 27-task reference frame (Suzgun et al., 2022) is given below; the **paper-specific subset and category assignment are `TBD-by-source`**:\\n\\n```\\nBoolean Expressions          free-form / boolean string\\nCausal Judgement             MC\\nDate Understanding           MC\\nDisambiguation QA            MC\\nFormal Fallacies             MC\\nGeometric Shapes             MC\\nHyperbaton                   MC\\nLogical Deduction (3,5,7)    MC (3 tasks)\\nMovie Recommendation         MC\\nMultistep Arithmetic         free-form, numeric\\nNavigate                     MC (Yes/No)\\nObject Counting              free-form, numeric\\nPenguins in a Table          free-form, structured\\nReasoning about Colored Objects  MC\\nRuin Names                   MC\\nSalient Translation          free-form (also MC-able)\\nSnarks                       MC\\nSports Understanding         MC\\nTemporal Sequences           MC\\nTracking Shuffled Objects    MC (3 tasks: 3, 5, 7)\\nWeb of Lies                  MC (Yes/No)\\nWord Sorting                 free-form, list\\n```\\n\\n### 3.2 Prompt source (TBD-by-source)\\nCandidate sources: `lukaemon/bbh`, original BBH release, `OpenCompass bbh` loader, `HELM` BBH, or paper-supplied JSON. The source matters only insofar as the **same** prompt set is consumed by both scoring passes; any source difference is a confound.\\n\\n### 3.3 Shared artifact \\u2014 predicted-text cache\\nA single frozen JSONL cache, one record per instance:\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\\"task\\\": \\\"<BBH-task-name, TBD-by-source>\\\",\\n  \\\"instance_id\\\": \\\"<BBH-internal-id>\\\",\\n  \\\"prompt\\\": \\\"<exact CoT prompt sent to the model>\\\",\\n  \\\"response\\\": \\\"<exact decoded continuation>\\\",\\n  \\\"extracted_answer\\\": \\\"<answer string after paper's extraction regex>\\\",\\n  \\\"gold\\\": \\\"<BBH gold reference>\\\",\\n  \\\"seed\\\": <int>,\\n  \\\"temperature\\\": 0\\n}\\n```\\nThis cache is the **single shared artifact** for both scoring passes, guaranteeing identical bytes compared, identical chat-template application, identical answer extraction for EM.\\n\\n### 3.4 Planned stack (design-only)\\n- Python 3.12.3.\\n- MinED via Levenshtein (`python-Levenshtein` if offline-installable; pure-Python `O(nm)` DP fallback otherwise). Tokenization **`TBD-by-source`**.\\n- Statistics: `numpy` paired bootstrap, `scipy.stats.wilcoxon`, `kendalltau`, `spearmanr`, custom sign test. CIs via percentile bootstrap, 10,000 resamples on the 27 task-differences.\\n- No GPU; no model-inference runtime required at scoring time.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. Procedure\\n\\n### 4.1 Pass 1 \\u2014 Build the predicted-text cache\\nFor each task in the 23+4 list and each instance within:\\n1. Build the CoT prompt `P_{t,i}` from the paper's prompt source.\\n2. Run the base LLM greedily (temperature 0, fixed seed), with the paper's max-new-tokens cap.\\n3. Record `(prompt, response, extracted_answer)` and the gold reference into the JSONL cache.\\n\\nThe cache is **scoring-agnostic**: both passes below consume it and never call the model.\\n\\n### 4.2 Pass 2 \\u2014 EM scoring pass\\n1. For each record `r`, normalize `r.extracted_answer` and `r.gold` (lowercase, strip whitespace, collapse internal whitespace; normalization rule `TBD-by-source` to mirror the paper).\\n2. `em_i = 1` if normalized predicted `==` normalized gold, else `0`.\\n3. Per-task aggregate: `mean_t(em)`, `var_t(em)`, distinct-value count, empirical entropy.\\n4. MC tasks: compare canonical option letters; free-form tasks: compare the post-extraction string. Same rule for both scoring passes \\u2014 fixing only the EM target string.\\n\\n### 4.3 Pass 3 \\u2014 MinED scoring pass (with mandatory negative control)\\n**Standard MinED pass.**\\n1. For each record `r`, tokenize `r.extracted_answer` and `r.gold` per the paper's MinED tokenization (`TBD-by-source`).\\n2. Compute Levenshtein distance `d_i` over the chosen tokens.\\n3. `mined_i = 1 \\u2212 d_i / max(len(pred_tokens), len(gold_tokens))`, clamped to `[0, 1]`. Empty-string guards `TBD-by-source`.\\n4. Per-task aggregate: `mean_t(mined)`, `var_t(mined)`, distinct-value count, empirical entropy.\\n\\n**Mandatory negative control \\u2014 forced-EM rerun of the MinED code path.**\\nRe-execute the MinED code with the Levenshtein DP replaced by an exact-equality token comparison (zero distance iff `pred_tokens == gold_tokens`, else a value that makes `1 \\u2212 d/max(\\u00b7) = 0`). Result: on every instance, every task, `mined_forced_i == em_i` to machine precision. Any discrepancy halts the experiment with an error report.\\n\\n**Tokenization sensitivity appendix (robustness only).**\\nRepeat the MinED pass with both character-level and BPE-token-level Levenshtein (the two natural choices for the paper's tokenizer); record discrepancy. **Not** used for primary inference; **only** to expose sensitivity to the `TBD-by-source` choice.\\n\\n### 4.4 Pass 4 \\u2014 Quality-proxy scoring (Definition B only)\\nIf a paper-licensed proxy exists:\\n1. For each record, compute `q_i` per the paper's definition (candidates `TBD-by-source`: log-prob of gold under the frozen LLM; multi-sample echo agreement; human-rated subset).\\n2. Pair `q_i` with `em_i` and `mined_i` per instance.\\n\\n### 4.5 Pass 5 \\u2014 Aggregate and infer (no execution performed)\\nSee \\u00a75.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. Analysis plan\\n\\n### 5.1 Unit of pairing\\nEvery comparison is **paired on instance `i`**. For each instance, both `em_i` and `mined_i` are available; for Definition B, `q_i` is additionally available.\\n\\n### 5.2 Definition A \\u2014 discriminative power\\n- Per task `t`: `\\u0394^{A}_t = Var_t(MinED) \\u2212 Var_t(EM)`; auxiliary `\\u0394^{A,ent}_t`, `\\u0394^{A,card}_t`.\\n- Across the 27 tasks:\\n  - **Primary**: paired bootstrap, 10,000 resamples, percentile 95% CI on mean `\\u0394^{A}_t` (tasks resampled with replacement).\\n  - **Robustness**: Wilcoxon signed-rank on `\\u0394^{A}_t`.\\n- **Stratification**: separately for the 23-task MC subset and the 4-task free-form subset; reported descriptively and inferentially as sub-family tests (n = 4 treated descriptively on its own).\\n\\n### 5.3 Definition B \\u2014 agreement with a quality proxy\\n- Per task `t`: `\\u03c4^{EM}_t = KendallTau_b(em_t, q_t)`, `\\u03c4^{MIN}_t = KendallTau_b(mined_t, q_t)`; `\\u0394^{B}_t = |\\u03c4^{MIN}_t| \\u2212 |\\u03c4^{EM}_t|`.\\n- **Primary**: paired bootstrap (10,000 resamples) of mean `\\u0394^{B}_t` across the 27 tasks; percentile 95% CI.\\n- **Robustness**: Wilcoxon signed-rank on `\\u0394^{B}_t`; sign test on `sign(\\u0394^{B}_t)` (McNemar-style).\\n- **Stratification**: identical to Definition A.\\n\\n### 5.4 Multiple-comparison handling\\n- A and B are reported in **separate families**; no pooled family-wise test across them.\\n- Within each family, the three statistics are descriptively reported; only the **primary** statistic's bootstrap CI carries the inferential claim.\\n- Subset analyses are descriptive; no post-hoc adjustments are pre-registered.\\n\\n### 5.5 Pre-registered decision rule (TBD-by-source)\\nDefer to the paper. Placeholder rules, **not binding**:\\n- Definition A: declare if 95% CI on mean `\\u0394^{A}_t` is strictly above 0 and Wilcoxon two-sided `p \\u2264 0.05` with rank-biserial \\u2265 0.5.\\n- Definition B: declare if 95% CI on mean `\\u0394^{B}_t` is strictly above 0 and sign test two-sided `p \\u2264 0.05`.\\n\\n### 5.6 Result-section structure (no numbers)\\n1. Negative-control outcome (forced-EM == EM must hold).\\n2. Definition A per-task deltas, stratification, bootstrap CI, Wilcoxon `p`.\\n3. Definition B per-task deltas, sign test; reported as \\\"incomplete\\\" if no paper-licensed proxy exists.\\n4. Tokenization-sensitivity appendix.\\n5. Threats-to-validity walk-through before any interpretive claim.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 6. Threats to validity\\n1. **Tokenization sensitivity for MinED (char vs. BPE).** Mitigated by the dual-pass robustness appendix; the paper's choice is mirrored as the primary.\\n2. **Prompt-template drift across scoring passes.** Mitigated by the same prompt source and the frozen JSONL cache that records `prompt` per record.\\n3. **Free-form answer-extraction aggressiveness.** A single fixed extraction regex feeds both passes, so the bias cancels within-pairs but conditions absolute magnitudes. Documented.\\n4. **Machine-precision determinism.** The forced-EM negative control is the primary defense; LSB-level disagreement is treated as a coding bug, halts inference. Greedy decoding makes cache-build reproducible.\\n5. **Multiple-comparison pollution across A, B, and stratified subsets.** A and B are separate families; within-family primary-statistic discipline; stratification treated descriptively.\\n6. **Ecological validity of the quality proxy (Definition B).** Definition B is secondary to a proxy-free Definition A; proxies are kept `TBD-by-source`; if no proxy is paper-licensed, Definition B is reported as \\\"incomplete\\\".\\n7. **Construction bias from `MinED \\u2265 EM`.** The design refuses raw-mean comparison; Definition A pre-registered as primary; explicit guardrail in \\u00a77 of the experimental protocol.\\n8. **Single-model / single-seed conditioning.** Results are conditional on paper's LLM and seed; cross-family generalization is out of scope.\\n9. **Empty-string and tie-handling edge cases in MinED.** Guards `TBD-by-source` from paper; edge cases enumerated.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. Feasibility\\n\\n### 7.1 Status\\nDesign-only. **No experiment has been executed. No command in this document is asserted to have been run.** The sandbox contains only `task.json`; no source PDF, no model weights, no dataset, no project dependencies installed.\\n\\n### 7.2 Scoring-stage feasibility on a single CPU\\n- **Per-pair Levenshtein**: `O(L_pred\\u00b7L_gold)` time, `O(min(L_pred, L_gold))` memory (rolling-row). For BBH, `L_pred, L_gold \\u2272 max_new_tokens` \\u2014 sub-millisecond per instance in pure Python.\\n- **Per-task aggregate**: linear in `(num_instances \\u00d7 L_pred \\u00d7 L_gold)`; tens of seconds wall-clock per task for both passes on a single thread, given typical ~250 instances per task.\\n- **Bootstrap**: 10,000 resamples \\u00d7 27 tasks \\u00d7 `O(|task|)` reduction; a few minutes wall-clock; no GPU.\\n- **Memory**: predicted-text cache a few MB; Levenshtein DP negligible; bootstrap holding `10,000 \\u00d7 27` floats negligible.\\n- All operations are CPU-friendly, FFT-free, no parallel prefix-sums. **Single-CPU correctness is feasible and well-defined.**\\n\\n### 7.3 What would change if executed (out of scope)\\n- Pass 1 (cache build) is the heavy step: minutes-to-hours on CPU for a 7B-class model, hours-to-days on a GPU cluster for 70B-class. It scales with model size. **This design does not run it.**\\n- If the paper specifies multi-seed / multi-temperature averaging, the design would draw a fixed seed from the paper's pre-registration rather than inventing one; `TBD-by-source`.\\n- Definition B is gated on the paper-licensed quality proxy; without one, Definition B is reported as \\\"incomplete\\\".\\n- `scipy`/`numpy` not pre-installed and bubblewrap forbids installation in this submission, so even a feasibility validation run is out of scope here.\\n\\n### 7.4 Submission-contract statement\\n- **No result is claimed.** The deliverable is a design document, not an experimental report.\\n- **No computation is asserted to have happened.** All numbers in the protocol are structural (counts of tasks, asymptotic costs, decision-rule placeholders).\\n- **All paper-specific facts are flagged `TBD-by-source`**: MinED tokenization, base LLM, exact 23+4 split, Definition-A-vs-B primary, pre-registered effect-size threshold, quality proxy, seed/temperature policy.\\n- **The decoding-rule framing is fully retracted.** The independent variable sits only at the scoring step on identical frozen model outputs.\\n- **The negative control is mandated before any inference.** A failed negative control halts the experiment by contract.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Carry-forward compile-time list (`TBD-by-source`, auditable)\\n1. MinED tokenization rule (character vs. BPE-token Levenshtein).\\n2. Base LLM identity for BBH cache build.\\n3. Exact BBH 23+4 task list and category assignment.\\n4. BBH prompt source (`lukaemon/bbh`, `OpenCompass`, `HELM`, paper-supplied).\\n5. Whether Definition A or Definition B is the paper's primary operationalization of \\\"outperforms\\\".\\n6. Pre-registered effect-size threshold and decision rule.\\n7. Quality proxy for Definition B (log-prob-of-gold / multi-sample echo agreement / human-rated subset).\\n8. Seed-and-temperature policy (single fixed vs. seed-averaged).\\n\\nThis completes the design. Submitting for review.\", \"evidence\": \"Re-inspected /workspace; still contains only task.json. No PDF, no supplementary, no model weights, no datasets, no installed project dependencies are available. Network is disabled in the bubblewrap sandbox so the paper PDF for ICLR 2024 ID 18013 cannot be fetched from inside; consequently every paper-specific fact is marked TBD-by-source and bound to the paper, never substituted by the design. The approved plan accepted setup_10 (EM = Exact Matching) and setup_11 (MinED = Minimum Edit Distance) as authoritative scoring criteria, retracted the prior decoding-rule framing, and committed to a paired within-instance design over a 23 MC + 4 free-form BBH split with two pre-registered operational definitions of outperforms (A: gradedness/discrimination as primary; B: agreement with a quality proxy as secondary), a paired bootstrap on task-level Deltas with Wilcoxon as robustness and a McNemar-style sign test for B, stratification by task type, family-wise handling for A vs B, and a mandatory negative control in which the MinED code path is collapsed to EM and required to match within machine precision on every task. The deliverable above implements that plan as a complete design document organized into the seven sections the researcher requested (hypothesis and operationalization; variables and controls; materials including BBH task list, prompt source, and shared predicted-text cache; procedure for the EM pass, the MinED pass, and the forced-EM negative control; paired analysis plan with stratification and multiple-comparison handling plus a TBD-by-source decision rule; threats to validity covering all six items the researcher named plus construction bias and single-model conditioning; and feasibility showing single-CPU correctness with a sub-millisecond per-pair Levenshtein, a few-MB cache, and a few-minute bootstrap). No number is presented as if from a run; no command is asserted to have been executed; every paper-bound element is flagged TBD-by-source and listed once more at the end for auditability.\", \"assumptions\": [\"MinED is operationalized here as a normalized Levenshtein alignment score, of the form 1 - edit_distance(predicted, gold) / max(len(predicted), len(gold)), with the edit-distance tokenization (character vs. BPE token) flagged TBD-by-source to mirror the paper.\", \"EM is operationalized as an exact-match indicator on the normalized final extracted answer string vs. the gold string, returning 1 on equality and 0 otherwise; for MC tasks the canonical option-letter comparison is used.\", \"BBH evaluation set is operationalized as the papers 23 MC + 4 free-form configuration with the canonical 27-task reference frame (Suzgun et al., 2022) used only as a default enumeration; the exact paper-specific subset and category assignment are flagged TBD-by-source.\", \"Manipulation is restricted to the scoring step, with all generation-time variables (LLM weights, greedy decoding, CoT 3-shot prompt templates, max-new-tokens, RNG seed, per-instance predicted text bytes) held byte-identical across the two scoring passes.\", \"Definition A (gradedness/discrimination) is the pre-registered primary operationalization of outperforms because it does not depend on a quality proxy whose choice is itself paper-specific; Definition B (agreement with a quality proxy) is pre-registered as secondary.\", \"The forced-EM rerun of the MinED code path is treated as a strict pass-or-halt gate rather than a soft check; any disagreement with the original EM pass anywhere on BBH halts the experiment by contract.\"], \"uncertainties\": [\"TBD-by-source: tokenization rule for MinED (character-level vs. BPE-token-level Levenshtein).\", \"TBD-by-source: identity of the base LLM frozen for BBH cache build.\", \"TBD-by-source: exact BBH 23 + 4 task list and category assignment.\", \"TBD-by-source: BBH prompt source (lukaemon/bbh, OpenCompass, HELM, paper-supplied).\", \"TBD-by-source: whether the papers primary operationalization of outperforms is Definition A or Definition B.\", \"TBD-by-source: pre-registered effect-size threshold and decision rule for the outperforms call.\", \"TBD-by-source: which quality proxy (log-prob-of-gold, multi-sample echo agreement, human-rated subset) the paper licenses for Definition B.\", \"TBD-by-source: seed-and-temperature policy (single fixed vs. seed-averaged) for the frozen generations.\"]}", "origin": "completion"}, "llm_response_id": "chatcmpl-b421b273-540f-41f5-a082-1070bb26185a", "security_risk": "UNKNOWN", "kind": "ActionEvent", "source_event_index": 22}
